# Patterns are matched against each path in the build context, and a pattern without a
# separator matches only at the top level. `node_modules` and `__pycache__` on their own
# therefore missed every nested copy, which is why the globs below are explicit.

# ~181 MB per copy, and there is one per Claude Code agent worktree under .claude/. The deps
# stage of frontend/Dockerfile runs its own `npm ci`, so no copy is ever wanted in a context.
**/node_modules

# .claude/ holds the agent worktrees: 998 MB on this machine at 15 worktrees, which took the
# build context from ~45 MB to ~1 GB. Local build speed only - .gitignore keeps it off the
# VM - but every local `docker compose build` paid for it.
.claude/

**/.git

# backend/Dockerfile is `COPY backend/ ./backend/`, so without these the production image
# shipped 176 KB of cpython-314 bytecode into a python:3.12-slim image, where it is not even
# loadable. Both test services bind-mount the repo (`.:/app`), which .dockerignore does not
# affect, so excluding tests from the images does not stop anyone running them.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
backend/test_*.py

# frontend/Dockerfile is `COPY frontend/public/ /usr/share/nginx/html/`, which published this
# on the production origin: GET /identify.test.js answered 200. It is run from the repo by
# `npm test`, never from the image.
frontend/public/*.test.js

# Deliberately NOT excluding test/, tools/, docs/, scripts/ or .github/ wholesale. They are
# only a few MB next to the two entries above, and a blanket exclusion is the kind of thing
# that makes a future `COPY test/ ...` copy nothing at all, with no error - which is the
# failure shape this file is being fixed to avoid.

.certs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
